lternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1002/batt.202400312"}],"type":"Article","urls":["http://dx.doi.org/10.1002/BATT.202400312"],"publicationDate":"2024-01-01","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn___print::20516cf76964013dac3e2459ef2440c8","value":"Batteries & Supercaps"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"re3data_____::c4b2081b224be6b3e79d0e5e5556f631","value":"European Union Open Data Portal"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1002/batt.202400312"}],"license":"CC BY","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["http://dx.doi.org/10.1002/batt.202400312"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn___print::20516cf76964013dac3e2459ef2440c8","value":"Batteries & Supercaps"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::a8db6f6b2ce4fe72e8b2314a9a93e7d9","value":"Sygma"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1002/batt.202400312"},{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.5445/ir/1000174239"}],"license":"CC BY","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/https://doi.org/10.1002/batt.202400312","https://doi.org/https://doi.org/10.5445/IR/1000174239"],"publicationDate":"2024-09-16","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::950a4152c2b4aa3ad78bdd6b366cc179","value":"KITopen (Karlsruhe Institute of Technologie)"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::df45502607927471ecf8a6ae83683ff5","value":"Bielefeld Academic Search Engine (BASE)"}}],"links":[{"header":{"relationType":"resultProject","relationClass":"isProducedBy","relatedIdentifier":"corda_____he::cac6f3787a39e1368ea44451e76955c6","relatedRecordType":"project","relationProvenance":"sysimport:crosswalk","trust":"0.9"},"collectedfrom":[{"dsId":"openaire____::3f264f93cf3b0cfc4ede188a6300455c","dsName":"CORDA - COmmon Research DAta Warehouse - Horizon Europe"}],"projectTitle":"Nanoporous and redox-active hoops and macrocycles as organic electrode materials for batteries","code":"101088146","funding":{"funder":{"id":"ec__________::EC","shortname":"EC","name":"European Commission","jurisdiction":{"code":"EU","label":"European Union"},"pid":null},"level0":{"id":"ec__________::EC::HE","description":"Horizon Europe Framework Programme","name":"HE"},"level1":{"id":"ec__________::EC::HE::ERC","description":"European Research Council","name":"ERC"},"level2":{"id":"ec__________::EC::HE::ERC::HORIZON-ERC","description":"HORIZON ERC Grants","name":"HORIZON-ERC"}},"startDate":"2023-11-01","endDate":"2028-10-31"}],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":true,"isGreen":true,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::394db7d4b8e7d82844c1384dccce2bec","fullName":"Longlong Wang","name":"Longlong","surname":"Wang","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-0873-7405"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Guy Rahamim","name":"Guy","surname":"Rahamim","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Kirankumar Vudutta","name":"Kirankumar","surname":"Vudutta","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::6ce865427fa4459645846a13b7b657a1","fullName":"Nicole Leifer","name":"Nicole","surname":"Leifer","rank":4,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-1708-8585"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Ran Elazari","name":"Ran","surname":"Elazari","rank":5,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Ilan Behar","name":"Ilan","surname":"Behar","rank":6,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Malachi Noked","name":"Malachi","surname":"Noked","rank":7,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::d8aad0d6454636a84187226c3aa3241b","fullName":"David Zitoun","name":"David","surname":"Zitoun","rank":8,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-3383-6165"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":"hybrid","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0202 electrical engineering, electronic engineering, information engineering"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"02 engineering and technology"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"7. Clean energy"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Influence of the Halogen in Argyrodite Electrolytes on the Electrochemical Performance of All‐Solid‐State Lithium Batteries","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:sec><jats:label/><jats:p>All‐solid‐state lithium batteries (ASSLBs) are considered as an alternative solution to lithium‐ion batteries, because of their safety and high theoretical energy density. Argyrodite‐based solid‐electrolytes (SEs), Li<jats:sub>6</jats:sub>PS<jats:sub>5</jats:sub>X (X = Cl, Cl<jats:sub>0.5</jats:sub>Br<jats:sub>0.5</jats:sub> or Br), are promising candidates for ASSLBs. Most of the previous reports have used Li<jats:sub>6</jats:sub>PS<jats:sub>5</jats:sub>Cl as the default SE composition. Here, the electrochemical behavior of three different argyrodites with Cl<jats:sup>−</jats:sup> or Br<jats:sup>−</jats:sup>, or both, as the halogen is systematically studied. Using LiNi<jats:sub>0.6</jats:sub>Co<jats:sub>0.2</jats:sub>Mn<jats:sub>0.2</jats:sub>O<jats:sub>2</jats:sub> as a model cathode, the behavior of these SEs in ASSLB cells is also studied. SEs containing Br show higher near‐room‐temperature ionic conductivity (&gt;2 mS cm<jats:sup>−1</jats:sup>) and the critical current density (≥1 mA cm<jats:sup>−2</jats:sup>) during Li plating/stripping, and are stable up to 5 V versus Li/Li<jats:sup>+</jats:sup>. Li<jats:sub>6</jats:sub>PS<jats:sub>5</jats:sub>Br gives the best electrochemical performance in terms of C‐rate and long‐term cycling among the three samples. Specifically, the cathode delivers an initial reversible capacity of 156 mAh g<jats:sup>−1</jats:sup>, with ≈27% irreversible capacity loss and 90% capacity retention over 100 cycles, and &gt;99% Coulombic efficiency. It delivers ≈56 mAh g<jats:sup>−1</jats:sup> at 10C, 36% of its initial capacity at 0.2C, whereas Li<jats:sub>6</jats:sub>PS<jats:sub>5</jats:sub>Cl and Li<jats:sub>6</jats:sub>PS<jats:sub>5</jats:sub>Cl<jats:sub>0.5</jats:sub>Br<jats:sub>0.5</jats:sub> deliver only 20 and 46 mAh g<jats:sup>−1</jats:sup> at 10C.</jats:p></jats:sec>"],"publicationDate":"2023-01-11","publisher":"Wiley","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Energy Technology","issnPrinted":"2194-4288","issnOnline":"2194-4296","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":null,"vol":"11","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_________::3b13ef71c866ba246fd3c3e5775f8513","originalIds":["10.1002/ente.202201116","50|doiboost____|3b13ef71c866ba246fd3c3e5775f8513"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1002/ente.202201116"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":5.0,"influence":2.2862097E-9,"popularity":5.051924E-9,"impulse":5.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C4","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Bar-Ilan University","acronym":"BIU","id":"openorgs____::99e089e1450a158fe723e80d9f79fa10","pids":[{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100002988"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100002744"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100002744"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.22098.31"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"521509"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100011735"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100002988